  "qualifications": [
    "S04 SVGAnimatedBoolean is declared but has no selected returner in Native18. Its real preserveAlpha provider belongs to next Native19; full S04 stays open. Twenty-five added handle roots do not mean twenty-five reachable instances.",
    "Native list method results retain stable managed wrapper identity; Chromium returns fresh wrappers aliasing the same live underlying values. Both enforce strong bidirectional mutations, detach and cross-list cloning. SameObject property checks remain exact.",
    "Unrestricted DOMMatrix2DInit coefficients remain unrestricted natively; the browser adapter requires genuine SVGMatrix and finite coefficient copies. This measured browser qualification is explicit; scalar SVG float/double inputs reject nonfinite values.",
    "NativeAOT child OS=Windows_NT restores the actual Windows host value only for publish; no unsupported-error suppression or global setting. Original netstandard and cross-OS publish failures are preserved.",
    "Initial orchestration marker spellings were wrong after successful child exits. Per-module counts and teardown were validated from preserved logs without rerunning unchanged AOT.",
    "Operational lease deviation remains separately recorded in artifacts/svg-operational-deviation.json. Subsequent operations carry inspected owner/kind/workdir lease receipts and terminal release records.",
    "All evidence is private coherent Windows ABI26 and packaged Chromium. Official package-only consumption, ordered release/pin replacement, remaining platforms/profiles and public acceptance remain open.",
    "Native cached wrappers retain their first acquisition receiver. Cache hits do not replace that anchor with every later list owner. Retained-list ownership is proven; item-only retention of a later owner is not promised. Engine owner destruction detaches a retained item, which remains usable under engine rules while its host lives."
  ]
}
